Aztlán is the sixth planet from the star Aurelius, orbiting beyond the habitable world [[Adonia]] and before the frozen frontier of [[Cíbola]]. It is a small, terrestrial planet roughly half the size of Adonia, distinguished by its vibrant rust-red coloration and the colossal tectonic fracture that scars its equator. It serves as the outermost boundary of the Inner System and is a frequent destination for robotic exploration due to its geological similarities to early Adonia.

The planet is cold, arid, and dusty. Its thin atmosphere offers little protection from meteor impacts or radiation, yet it is thick enough to support massive, planet-wide dust storms that can obscure the surface for weeks. Aztlán is geologically dead compared to the active Adonia; its core has cooled significantly, resulting in a weak magnetic field that has allowed the solar wind to strip away much of its ancient atmosphere.

Aztlán is most famous for the Gran Grieta Escarlata (Great Scarlet Chasm), a canyon system so massive it is visible from simple telescopes on Adonia. This feature suggests a violent tectonic past where the planet's crust nearly tore itself apart during the cooling phase.

==Physical characteristics==
===Surface geology===
The surface of Aztlán is covered in a fine regolith of iron oxide dust, giving it a distinctive salmon-red hue. Underneath this dust lies a thick crust of basaltic rock. The planet is divided into two distinct hemispheres: the smooth, low-lying northern plains, which may be the basin of an ancient ocean, and the rugged, heavily cratered southern highlands.

The dominant feature is the Gran Grieta Escarlata, a tectonic crack system that spans nearly 4,000 kilometers in length and reaches depths of up to 7 kilometers. Unlike river valleys formed by erosion, this chasm was formed by crustal stress. Other geological features include the Olympus Montes, a chain of extinct shield volcanoes that dwarf the largest mountains on [[Adonia]]. While no longer active, their lava flows remain preserved in the vacuum-like conditions.

===Atmosphere===
Aztlán possesses a very tenuous atmosphere composed mostly of carbon dioxide. The atmospheric pressure is less than 1% of Adonia's, meaning liquid water cannot exist on the surface; it would instantly boil away or freeze. However, evidence of ancient riverbeds and delta fans suggests that the atmosphere was once much thicker and warmer, possibly supported by the greenhouse gases released during the formation of the great volcanoes.

The sky of Aztlán appears a butterscotch color during the day due to suspended dust particles. Sunsets are famously blue, a reversal of the visual palette seen on Adonia.

==Orbit and rotation==
Aztlán orbits Aurelius at an average distance of 1.55 AU, completing a revolution every 710 standard days, almost exactly two Adonian years. This 2:1 resonance is coincidental but makes calendar conversions simple for Adonian astronomers.

The planet rotates on its axis once every 24.6 hours, a day length remarkably similar to [[Adonia]]. Its axial tilt is 25 degrees, resulting in seasons similar to those on the homeworld, though they last twice as long. During the southern summer, the sublimation of the carbon dioxide ice caps can trigger global dust storms that raise the atmospheric temperature significantly.

==Name and etymology==
The name Aztlán is derived from Insulonian mythology, referring to the ancestral home of the peoples, often depicted as a land of red earth and lakes. The name was chosen to reflect the planet's reddish appearance and the scientific theory that it may have harbored liquid water billions of years before Adonia.

In Sanese astronomical nomenclature, the planet is known as Hikyōsei (緋峡星), translating to the Scarlet Canyon Star. This name references the Gran Grieta Escarlata, emphasizing the violent geology that defines the world's face.

